    TEST-0010: test checkout with test doubles
    
    The tests hand checkout() stand-ins for CoastPay, so nobody is charged:
    
    - ApprovingProcessor and DecliningProcessor always give the same
      answer, so each test picks the outcome it needs.
    - RecordingProcessor remembers every amount it's asked to charge, so a
      test can check that checkout() charged the price of the offering, in
      cents.
    
    All three keep PaymentProcessor's contract: they return true or false,
    and never throw.
    
    The expected amount comes from the real priceFor(). It's fast, gives
    the same answer every time, and has no side effects, so there's no
    reason to replace it.

